Okay, here are some strategies:
SPOILERS

1) Don't advance too fast.  If you have plenty of food, just check the
   first four levels for shops and then retreat, waiting for the critters
   to bring you good stuff.  Not very exciting, but ...
2) The above goes double if you find an altar.  It's almost essential to
   hang by an altar #offering carcasses just as soon as you find an altar,
   just to get a good weapon.
3) In absence of an altar, you can often get a good weapon/armor from the
   spoils left by orc/elf hordes or from dwarves.  Hard shoes + chain mail
   + orcish helm is AC2 already; not so bad!  Sell all the armor and the
   weapons you find to the shopkeepers; they will offer you an extra 5 gp
   per enchantment.  It's not at all unusual to find a +2 curved sword;
    which is quite a decent weapon.
4) A pickaxe from an ex-dwarf can be used to deal with any single annoying
   monster quite well, like a unicorn or nymph.  Dig a pit, get the critter
   to fall in it, and pepper it with sharp things at your leisure.
5) Fight large groups of monsters by retreating into a hallway.
6) Get ESP by eating a floating eye ASAP.  Use blindfold for radar.
7) Kill unicorn to get horn which cures all.  You'll get pois res
   very soon cause you can eat poison corpses and gain str back with
   the horn.
8) It's not supposed to be _real_ easy anyhow.
9) Anything else specific you want to know?


